# Two clients of one server, on a device that queues
# (`app.new(…).offline(.Queue)`). The phone saves two tasks; the test host
# cuts it off (`app.disconnect`), and its two renames wait in the queue
# (`app.pending()` is 2) while each call succeeds at once. The desk removes
# the second task. `app.reconnect("phone")` sends the queue in order: the
# server commits the first rename and refuses the second (its task is
# gone), so the phone rolls that write back. It leaves the queue, which is
# empty after, and the desk reads the first rename and no second task.
# Same output on O0, O1 and O2.
fixture: SyncTwoClients.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step o0: jet run -O0 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "phone saved, pending: 0\nphone cut off, pending: 2\ndesk reads: plan, none\nphone reconnected, pending: 0\ndesk reads: plan v2, none\n"
step o1: jet run -O1 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == o0
step o2: jet run -O2 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == o0
